From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ran Wang <wangra@google.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:15:04 -0400
Subject: D3D11: Fix stale vertex and index buffer pointers

Clear cached D3D11 vertex and index buffer pointers on invalidation
and buffer release, keep state updates atomic on errors, and propagate
vertex array binding dirty bits across shared attributes.

Test:
    angle_end2end_tests --gtest_filter="*DeletedVertexBufferBeforeInternalDraw*:*VertexBufferOffsetOverflowRecovery*"
Bug: b/568897206
Change-Id: I9f10aae425328e514359c4008fe31f3fa05c2901
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8520817
Reviewed-by: Yuxin Hu <yuxinhu@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Ran Wang <wangra@google.com>

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y): Renderer11's constructor on this
revision still initializes mScratchMemoryBuffer, so mResourceManager11(this)
is added alongside it in declaration order; the enabled-attribute early
`continue` in StateManager11::syncCurrentValueAttribs had no braces here and
was resolved to upstream's braced form with the
mDirtyCurrentValueAttribs.reset() call. VertexAttributeTest hunks did not
apply and were dropped.

